# Procedural Meshes and Generated Assets

Generators are DISPOSABLE tools. Their OUTPUT is permanent project data.
The user will generate an environment through the Inspector, review it, and later DELETE the generator scripts.
Therefore the result must never depend on temporary in-memory objects or on the generator scripts.

## Core principle
- NEVER leave geometry only as runtime/in-memory meshes. Every generated Mesh, Material, Texture, and Prefab
  must be saved as a real asset under `Assets/Generated/`.
- The saved prefab must still work after the generator and editor scripts are deleted.

## Output layout

```
Assets/Generated/
  {Feature}/
    Meshes/       # .asset  -> {OutputName}_Mesh_000.asset
    Materials/    # .mat    -> {OutputName}_Mat_000.mat
    Textures/     # .png / .asset
    Prefabs/      # .prefab -> {OutputName}.prefab
```

- `Assets/Generated/` holds output data ONLY. Never put scripts there.
- `{OutputName}` defaults to the generator name and is exposed as a serialized string on the generator.
- Names are deterministic. Re-generating OVERWRITES the same assets in place so GUIDs and references stay stable
  (no `_1`, `_2` duplicates). Only touch assets that start with this generator's `{OutputName}`.
- Create folders with `AssetDatabase.CreateFolder` (never `System.IO` directly) so Unity tracks them.

## Self-contained output (safe to delete the generator)
- Saved prefabs may contain ONLY built-in components (Transform, MeshFilter, MeshRenderer, colliders, LODGroup, ...)
  or components from permanent runtime scripts. They must NOT reference the generator component, the editor script,
  or any script the user plans to delete.
- Materials reference shaders or materials, never generator scripts.
- The generator component itself stays on the scene object only. The user removes it before deleting the scripts.
- In the change summary, state explicitly whether the generated prefab depends on any script (it should say "No").

## Editor buttons (extends 02-environment-generators)
- **Generate** - builds in the scene as a preview (in-memory is OK here).
- **Generate & Save Assets** - generates, saves all meshes/materials/textures as assets, re-points the scene objects to the saved assets, and saves the prefab.
- **Clear** - removes the scene container only. NEVER deletes anything in `Assets/Generated/`.
- Optional **Ping Output Folder**: `EditorGUIUtility.PingObject(AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<Object>(folder))`.

## Shared helper (create once, reuse)
- Put the saving logic in ONE shared editor helper: `Assets/Editor/Core/GeneratedAssetSaver.cs`.
- Before creating it, check whether it already exists. Reuse and extend it. Do not duplicate it per generator.
- It is shared infrastructure, so in the summary mark it "Keep (shared helper)", NOT safe to delete.
- Generators call the helper from the editor script only. Runtime scripts must not reference `AssetDatabase`.

## Mesh rules
- Build with `Mesh.SetVertices / SetTriangles / SetUVs / SetNormals` (or `MeshData` for heavy cases). Always set `mesh.name`.
- Winding: Unity front faces are CLOCKWISE when viewed from the front. Wrong winding causes invisible or inside-out faces.
- Use `mesh.indexFormat = IndexFormat.UInt32` when vertices exceed 65,535.
- Call `RecalculateBounds()`. Call `RecalculateNormals()` unless you set normals yourself. Add UVs and `RecalculateTangents()` if materials use normal maps.
- Reuse one mesh for identical shapes instead of creating a copy per object. Merge static pieces when it reduces object count.
- For colliders, assign saved meshes to `MeshCollider.sharedMesh`. Prefer primitive colliders when possible.
- Never create meshes in `Update`. Destroy leftover in-memory meshes after saving (`DestroyImmediate`) to avoid leaks.
- Mention the vertex/triangle budget in the summary for large outputs.

## Material and texture rules
- Do not guess shader names. Check `Packages/manifest.json` and `ProjectSettings/GraphicsSettings.asset` context to see if
  the project is Built-in, URP, or HDRP. Prefer a serialized base `Material` field on the generator and create saved variants from it.
- Procedural textures: save as `.png` (`EncodeToPNG`) into `Textures/` then `AssetDatabase.ImportAsset`; set import settings via `TextureImporter` if needed.
- Share materials between objects. Do not create one material per object.

## Template: shared editor helper

```csharp
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using UnityEditor;
using UnityEngine;

namespace MyGame.Core.Editor
{
    public static class GeneratedAssetSaver
    {
        public const string Root = "Assets/Generated";

        public static string GetFolder(string feature, string kind) // kind: Meshes, Materials, Textures, Prefabs
        {
            string path = $"{Root}/{feature}/{kind}";
            EnsureFolder(path);
            return path;
        }

        public static void EnsureFolder(string path)
        {
            if (AssetDatabase.IsValidFolder(path)) return;
            string parent = Path.GetDirectoryName(path).Replace('\\', '/');
            EnsureFolder(parent);
            AssetDatabase.CreateFolder(parent, Path.GetFileName(path));
        }

        // Creates the asset, or overwrites it in place so the GUID stays stable.
        public static T SaveOrUpdate<T>(T source, string path) where T : Object
        {
            var existing = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<T>(path);
            if (existing == null)
            {
                AssetDatabase.CreateAsset(source, path);
                return source;
            }
            EditorUtility.CopySerialized(source, existing);
            EditorUtility.SetDirty(existing);
            return existing;
        }

        // Saves every in-memory mesh/material under 'root' as assets, re-points the scene objects,
        // then saves a prefab named 'baseName'. Returns the prefab asset.
        public static GameObject BakeToPrefab(GameObject root, string feature, string baseName)
        {
            var leftovers = new List<Object>();
            var meshMap = new Dictionary<Mesh, Mesh>();
            var matMap = new Dictionary<Material, Material>();
            int meshIndex = 0, matIndex = 0;

            foreach (var mf in root.GetComponentsInChildren<MeshFilter>(true))
            {
                var m = mf.sharedMesh;
                if (m == null || AssetDatabase.Contains(m)) continue;
                if (!meshMap.TryGetValue(m, out var saved))
                {
                    string path = $"{GetFolder(feature, "Meshes")}/{baseName}_Mesh_{meshIndex++:000}.asset";
                    saved = SaveOrUpdate(m, path);
                    if (saved != m) leftovers.Add(m);
                    meshMap[m] = saved;
                }
                mf.sharedMesh = saved;
            }

            foreach (var r in root.GetComponentsInChildren<Renderer>(true))
            {
                var mats = r.sharedMaterials;
                for (int i = 0; i < mats.Length; i++)
                {
                    var mat = mats[i];
                    if (mat == null || AssetDatabase.Contains(mat)) continue;
                    if (!matMap.TryGetValue(mat, out var saved))
                    {
                        string path = $"{GetFolder(feature, "Materials")}/{baseName}_Mat_{matIndex++:000}.mat";
                        saved = SaveOrUpdate(mat, path);
                        if (saved != mat) leftovers.Add(mat);
                        matMap[mat] = saved;
                    }
                    mats[i] = saved;
                }
                r.sharedMaterials = mats;
            }

            // Save a clean copy so the prefab root is named after the asset, not "[Generated]".
            var copy = Object.Instantiate(root);
            copy.transform.SetParent(null);
            copy.transform.SetPositionAndRotation(Vector3.zero, Quaternion.identity);
            copy.transform.localScale = Vector3.one;
            copy.name = baseName;

            string prefabPath = $"{GetFolder(feature, "Prefabs")}/{baseName}.prefab";
            var prefab = PrefabUtility.SaveAsPrefabAsset(copy, prefabPath);
            Object.DestroyImmediate(copy);

            foreach (var o in leftovers) if (o != null) Object.DestroyImmediate(o);

            AssetDatabase.SaveAssets();
            AssetDatabase.Refresh();
            return prefab;
        }
    }
}
```

## Template: button in the generator's editor script

```csharp
if (GUILayout.Button("Generate & Save Assets", GUILayout.Height(28)))
    Run(generator, "Generate & Save Example", () =>
    {
        generator.Generate();
        var container = generator.transform.Find(ExampleGenerator.ContainerName);
        if (container != null)
            GeneratedAssetSaver.BakeToPrefab(container.gameObject, "Environment", generator.OutputName);
    });
```

(Asset creation is not covered by Undo. Mention this in the summary.)

## Done checklist for generators that create geometry
- [ ] Meshes, materials, textures, and prefab are saved under `Assets/Generated/{Feature}/...`
- [ ] Re-running overwrites in place (no duplicate assets)
- [ ] The saved prefab has no reference to the generator or editor scripts
- [ ] Summary has a "Safe to delete after generating" section and a "Keep" section
